---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About and credits" description="Who curates Endrheim, what the name means, and the people whose mods make it.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <h1>About and credits</h1>

    <section aria-labelledby="name-title">
      <h2 id="name-title">The name</h2>
      <p>
        Endrheim joins two Old Norse words: <i lang="non">endr</i>, “again”, and <i lang="non">heimr</i>, “world”.
        In the <i>Völuspá</i>, the earth rises from the sea once more after Ragnarök, green and renewed. That is the idea behind the list: the same Skyrim, made new.
        The emblem is Dagaz, the rune of dawn, which is also the D in the name.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="curator-title">
      <h2 id="curator-title">Curation</h2>
      <p>[Placeholder: a few lines from Peter about the goals of the list and how it was built and tested.]</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="credits-title">
      <h2 id="credits-title">Credits</h2>
      <p>
        Endrheim stands on the work of the mod authors listed on the <a href="/mods">mod list</a>.
        Their mods are downloaded from their original pages during installation and are never redistributed here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="support-title">
      <h2 id="support-title">Support</h2>
      <p>Endrheim is free. [Placeholder: optional PayPal donation link, added at release. Please consider supporting the mod authors first.]</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 4rem; }
  section { margin-top: 3rem; }
</style>
